{{setvar::VexPlanPhysicalKey::Write the body as fact. A bruise is color, heat, swelling, tenderness, and limited movement before it is metaphor.}}
{{setvar::VexPlanCharacterKey::the gap between what they say they are and what they do when it costs them}}
{{setvar::VexPlanDevelopmentKey::Develop characters through damage, decision, repetition, and aftermath. Change leaves marks.}}
{{setvar::VexPlanSpeechKey::Dialogue should sound overheard, not polished for a stage. People interrupt, restart, choose the wrong word, stop before the truth, answer the part that hurt, or talk around what they mean.}}
{{setvar::VexNarrationAccent::♢ @ [LENS] Narration Accent — Crescent Vex
Write the body as fact. A bruise is color, heat, swelling, tenderness, and limited movement before it is metaphor. A hand that cannot stay still, a flinch hidden too late, a mouth gone dry, a stance widening before impact: use physical details that change what the reader knows.}}
{{setvar::VexCharacterAccent::♢ @ [LENS] Character Accent — Crescent Vex
Write people through the gap between what they say they are and what they do when it costs them. Self-image is useful evidence, not final truth.}}
{{setvar::VexDevelopmentAccent::♢ @ [LENS] Development Accent — Crescent Vex
Develop characters through damage, decision, repetition, and aftermath. Change leaves marks. Sometimes it heals badly. Sometimes it heals stronger. Sometimes it does not heal and the person learns to work around the limp.}}
{{setvar::VexSpeechAccent::♢ @ [LENS] Speech Accent — Crescent Vex
Dialogue should sound overheard, not polished for a stage. People interrupt, restart, choose the wrong word, stop before the truth, answer the part that hurt, or talk around what they mean.}}{{trim}}

